  "visual_differences": {
    "g19": "Thursday 10:00, Dhuhr countdown, Masjid marker, buttons and values agree. Existing Godot map uses different label weight, outlines, gate rim, scale and canal label positions, marker placement and footer and HUD spacing.",
    "g25–g29": "The real daylight greybox at the Masjid replaces the prototype's nighttime quay image. The clock follows the existing daylight cutoff at 18:40. Fonts, tracking, panel translucency and height, line spacing, button widths and spacing, HUD widths and corner radii differ. Story, captions, counters, choices and replies use the approved data.",
    "g25/g27/g28": "Unknown words are blue, italic and underlined in Godot. The prototype uses a dotted underline. In g28, Ba‘d al-‘isha fits on one line in Godot. The beat and count of two follow the row 6 answer.",
    "g26": "The learned English appears in bold. The smaller town spelling in brackets uses the mixed case from the data. The prototype shows uppercase. The reply, New word notice and count of one agree.",
    "g29": "The revealed name, invitation, words-you-know count of three, Back to the market, Meet him again and Leave are visible in the approved order.",
    "supplemental": "The native Masjid entry at 10:00 shows Dhuhr in 2 h 5 min while retaining the After Maghrib caption. Arrival at 18:15 shows the live fair-Arrival wallet of 198 coins. The six paired captures use the pictured zero-coin state."
  },
